<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 29 November, from 618 to 1963.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/618">618 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,408 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Li Shimin destroys Xue Rengao's army at Qianshuiyuan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a>, the future Emperor Taizong of Tang, waited until the supplies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> state ran short and then destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xue-rengao">Xue Rengao</a>'s army at Qianshuiyuan, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a>. Xue Rengao surrendered and was executed, opening the north-west to the Tang.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qianshuiyuan">Battle of Qianshuiyuan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xue-rengao">Xue Rengao</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1114">1114 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">912 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A great earthquake strikes Marash and the crusader lands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake with an estimated magnitude of 7.4 to 7.7 struck the area of Marash, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahramanmaras">Kahramanmaraş</a>, and also hit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>, Mamistra and Edessa in the crusader lands. At least 40,000 people were killed, a figure historians contest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahramanmaras">Kahramanmaraş</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch-on-the-orontes">Antioch-on-the-Orontes</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1530">1530 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">496 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cardinal Wolsey dies on his way to face treason charges</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thomas Wolsey, once <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s all-powerful Lord Chancellor, died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leicester">Leicester</a> Abbey. He had fallen from favour after failing to obtain the annulment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s marriage to Catherine of Aragon.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1612">1612 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">414 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">English East India Company ships defeat the Portuguese off Swally</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The naval Battle of Swally, fought on 29 and 30 November off Suvali near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surat">Surat</a>, ended in victory for four <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">English East India Company</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galleon">galleons</a> over four Portuguese galleons and 26 barks. It loosened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>'s hold on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/cumberland" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cumberland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British reinforcements end the Patriot siege of Fort Cumberland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British reinforcements ended a siege of Fort <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumberland">Cumberland</a> by Patriot militia under Jonathan Eddy. With four to five hundred volunteers and Natives and little support from Massachusetts, Eddy had tried to bring the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Colorado troops massacre Cheyenne and Arapaho at Sand Creek</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonel John Chivington's volunteer cavalry attacked a peaceful camp at Sand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a>, killing about 150 to 200 people, mostly women, children and the elderly. Congressional inquiries condemned the attack.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1947">1947 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The UN votes to partition Palestine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The UN General Assembly adopted Resolution 181, recommending separate Jewish and Arab states with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> under international control. Fighting broke out the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Johnson sets up the Warren Commission</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President Lyndon Johnson appointed a commission under Chief Justice Earl Warren to investigate Kennedy's assassination. Its 1964 report concluded that Lee Harvey Oswald acted alone.</p></div></li></ol>
